  "2026-10-31T03:02:47.725Z",codex-agent,"Synchronized Bun stable pass: 708 Rust tests, 82 crash tests, zero failures/skips; history-prefix and retained-evidence gates passed. Instrumented pass reached 494 passed / 1 failed / 0 ignored, stopping on an existing assert_cmd runtime binary lookup before the create CLI test could execute. The nightly build layout needs CARGO_BIN_EXE_pm-rust set to the verified instrumented executable. Supplying that standard runtime location makes all 8 create-contract tests pass under instrumentation. Temporary runner corrected to supply the matching built binary as well as worker caps; restarting the full aggregate without changing product code, tests, assertions or thresholds."
  "2026-10-31T04:13:53.133Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-through: added shipped-binary regressions for malformed and unreadable scalar identity settings, and unavailable optional Git provenance in a real repository. All six focused CLI admission cases pass, including the retained closed-stdout test; the complete admission contract now contains eleven tests. Source opens now propagate each handle-relative failure to one uniform source refusal boundary, with no later component opened after failure. No dependency, threshold, or ownership policy changes. Aggregate rerun uses the current official cargo-llvm-cov release in an isolated tool directory; a runner only selects at most two test workers and the verified built binary location required by the newer nightly Cargo layout."
  "2026-10-31T04:14:14.686Z",codex-agent,"Final Source.read composition rechecked with a fresh function-only revert to e4c0d00 in a disposable non-git copy: parent-component swap test compiled and failed 0 passed / 1 failed when reverted; restoring the current source compiled and passed 1 / 0. The normal regular-source control remains in the same regression. Earlier ownership revert proof remains unchanged: reverted scalar guard 0 / 1, restored native plus published owner fixture 1 / 0."
  "2026-10-31T04:20:49.070Z",codex-agent,"Closed the test-artifact lookup class: fourteen create/read assert_cmd calls now use the Cargo-provided compile-time binary path, as the other native contract tests already do. The pinned nightly Cargo artifact layout invalidates runtime inference; this correction retains all assertions and allows CI to use its normal runner. Stopped the unfinished aggregate before changing its test harness, and will rerun both engine aggregates with immutable source. Removed the local binary-path override; the resource runner now only selects one worker for orientation differential tests and two elsewhere."
  "2026-10-31T04:22:09.766Z",codex-agent,"Final linked execution through pm test --run --progress: all nine commands passed, no skipped commands; 57 Rust tests passed with zero failures or ignored tests. Result recording is disabled by project policy, so this comment retains the receipt. Separately, the corrected create/read contracts ran under the pinned nightly, with its unmodified runner and without an injected binary-path environment variable: 26 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored. Both engine aggregates are now rerun with unchanged source, current cargo-llvm-cov, neutral HOME, and the worker-count-only local runner."
  "2026-10-31T04:45:46.524Z",codex-agent,"Crash corpus: 82 passed, 0 failed, cancelled, skipped or todo. History prefix check passes for all three main-owned streams and retained evidence check covers twenty receipts and thirty-six commits. Separately verified the existing Node lint-tool audit warning and recorded pm-rust-node-tooling-audit after checking the complete tracker for its advisory identifier and package name; no duplicate item was found. No dependency pins were changed."
  "2026-10-31T05:06:35.173Z",codex-agent,"Full Bun release:check passed on the final unchanged source: fmt, deny-warning Clippy, private documentation, 710 stable Rust tests, 82 crash checks, 710 nightly instrumented Rust tests, no failures or ignored/skipped cases. Global llvm-cov: 26570/26570 regions, 16138/16138 lines, 1689/1689 functions, 3690/3690 branches, all 100 percent. Cargo audit passed across 136 crate dependencies with its existing allowed unsafe-libyaml unmaintained warning; changelog check passed. Current official cargo-llvm-cov 0.9.1 was verified in an isolated tool directory. Both behavioral revert proofs and all nine linked commands (57 tests) passed their required controls. All three existing touched histories verified strictly (97, 6 and 12 entries at that checkpoint), matching the items. Final npm aggregate repeats the same recipe on this source alongside exact pushed-head CI; its completion and the final CI per-job receipt will be recorded in the PR and final report. Releasing only this implementation claim; keep all items nonterminal for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-31T05:13:58.468Z",codex-agent,"Head 362fed9 CI found a Windows-only handle lifetime issue in the new protected source read: 371 unit tests passed, including the parent-component swap regression, and three existing after-read interleaving tests failed because the leaf deny-write handle was still live when their competing writer ran. Close the leaf immediately after the bounded read, before caching and the after-read checkpoint; retain all no-follow and sharing protection during the read. Stopped the unfinished npm aggregate before modifying source. Reclaimed the implementation item for this repair; fresh exact-head CI and local aggregate validation will follow. Failed job receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/41171277451/job/124449557236"
  "2026-10-31T05:17:48.446Z",codex-agent,"Windows repair completed without relaxing traversal or sharing protections: Source.read closes its protected leaf immediately after the bounded read, before publishing cached bytes and invoking the after-read checkpoint. Both Windows failures on 362fed9 were the same 371 passed / 3 failed unit result, caused by the existing interleaving writer attempting to write through a still-held deny-write handle. Final correction passes 22 admission unit tests and all-target deny-warning Clippy locally. Re-executed every linked command through pm test --run --progress: 9 passed commands, 57 passed tests, 0 failures, ignored or skipped cases. Fresh final Source.read function-only revert to e4c0d00 compiled and failed the parent-swap regression 0 / 1; restoring the current correction compiled and passed 1 / 0. Ownership proof remains unchanged and valid. The earlier complete Bun result belongs to 362fed9; both complete local engine gates now repeat sequentially on the corrected immutable head alongside fresh Windows/macOS/Linux CI. Final exact-head gate and CI receipts will be published in the PR and final report. Release implementation claim without closing this item."
  "2026-10-31T06:30:59.452Z",claude-hub,"CodeRabbit round on dd85aee, fixed by hand. validate_scalar_owner now receives the caller principal from its call sites: native update and comment resolve caller_principal(author), which includes the scoped session, while prepare_update_preview passes the batch author only. Previews therefore never inherit an ambient AuthorIdentity, as the AdmissionBatch.author contract states. New test preview_ownership_ignores_an_ambient_scoped_identity: inside alpha's scope, a batch by intruder is refused with ownership_conflict, and alpha's own batch is admitted without a scope. It fails on revert (0/1). CI now sets CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 (CodeRabbit's outside-diff note). fmt, clippy -D warnings (all targets) and changelog-check pass; lib 382, admission 11, claim/release differential 27, close differential 6, mutation 29, ownership 11."
  "2026-10-31T07:30:29.763Z",claude-hub,"CodeRabbit round on df8012c (2 minor), fixed by hand. (1) New public AdmissionPreview::with_input_bytes replaces the canonical count and re-measures JSON and TOON against output_bytes. The CLI calls it inside the existing preview refusal boundary (one ?), so a stdin count with more digits can no longer push a receipt over 65,536 bytes. New test admission_input_byte_replacement_rechecks_the_output_ceiling binary-searches a receipt just under the ceiling and shows a 16-digit count is refused; it fails without the re-check (0/1). (2) The Windows source pin now opens ancestors with FILE_SHARE_READ|WRITE (delete still denied, so an ancestor cannot be renamed or replaced, while writers may link or rename children) and the leaf with FILE_SHARE_READ|DELETE (a native rename replacement succeeds; in-place writes stay blocked during the bounded read). New Windows-only test windows_source_pin_allows_child_links_and_leaf_replacement; it runs only on Windows CI and cross-compiled cleanly for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu. fmt, clippy -D warnings (native and Windows target), changelog-check; lib 382, admission 12, cli_dispatch 17."
